WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.177
Mother Teresa was born in 1910 in what is now the small country of Macedonia.

2
00:00:06.178 --> 00:00:10.381
When she was young, she was always happy to help out at church.

3
00:00:10.382 --> 00:00:14.273
She liked to borrow books from the priest.

4
00:00:14.274 --> 00:00:19.894
"May I read some of your books about missionaries?" she asked the priest one day.

5
00:00:19.895 --> 00:00:23.383
"Of course you may! Here they are," he said.

6
00:00:23.384 --> 00:00:29.303
She read the books over and over, and she was touched by the stories about caring for others.

7
00:00:29.304 --> 00:00:34.859
Her favorite book was about the missionaries who worked in India.

8
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:39.258
It made her think about caring for poor people in India herself.

9
00:00:39.259 --> 00:00:46.030
When Mother Teresa was 12, she asked God if she should go to India to help people as a missionary.

10
00:00:46.031 --> 00:00:48.666
She prayed about this for six years.

11
00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:52.861
When she was 18, she asked a priest about her prayers.

12
00:00:52.862 --> 00:00:56.474
"I have talked to my mother and my sisters about this.

13
00:00:56.475 --> 00:00:59.600
I have prayed a lot too.

14
00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:03.624
But how can I be sure that God wants me to go to India?"

15
00:01:03.625 --> 00:01:08.127
"You will know through your joy, my child," was his advice.

16
00:01:08.128 --> 00:01:14.027
"I would be very happy if God let me serve him and other people," she said.

17
00:01:14.028 --> 00:01:17.378
Mother Teresa knew that her heart was leading her.

18
00:01:17.379 --> 00:01:22.824
Soon after, she went to Dublin to learn English and to be trained as a nun.

19
00:01:22.825 --> 00:01:25.532
Then Mother Teresa was sent to India.

20
00:01:25.533 --> 00:01:28.821
There she learned to speak Hindi and Bengali.

21
00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:32.163
She was saddened by the way most people lived in India.

22
00:01:32.164 --> 00:01:37.828
Most people were very poor. "Oh! Look at what little they have to eat!

23
00:01:37.829 --> 00:01:44.543
How can I help them?" she wondered. "So many people here are poor."

24
00:01:44.544 --> 00:01:50.226
While she worked very hard to help the poor, she also taught children at a high school.

25
00:01:50.227 --> 00:01:57.224
After a few years, she became the school principal, but the suffering of the poor was never far from her mind.

26
00:01:57.225 --> 00:02:07.178
"God, I know that being a school principal is an important job because I can help poor children to learn.

27
00:02:07.179 --> 00:02:10.980
But who takes care of the poor people who live on the streets?

28
00:02:10.981 --> 00:02:13.949
How can I help them too?" she prayed.

29
00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:20.056
On September 10, 1946, Mother Teresa felt that God had given her an answer.

30
00:02:20.057 --> 00:02:25.195
She was sure that he wanted her to serve him by helping the poorest of the poor.

31
00:02:25.196 --> 00:02:31.482
She thanked him for answering her prayer. "I know what I must do now.

32
00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:36.440
I must live with the poorest people, but how can I help them best?"

33
00:02:36.441 --> 00:02:38.619
She decided to become a nurse.

34
00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:45.525
One day, as she was walking on a street in the slums of Calcutta, she saw a woman lying in the dirt.

35
00:02:45.526 --> 00:02:54.555
"Oh! She might be hurt!" Mother Teresa thought. "Are you okay?" she asked.

36
00:02:54.556 --> 00:02:57.715
"Oh . . .," the woman groaned.

37
00:02:57.716 --> 00:03:00.947
Mother Teresa was shocked at the woman's condition.

38
00:03:00.948 --> 00:03:06.549
"Oh, how terrible! Look at all the rats and ants around this woman!

39
00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:13.032
Please, help me! I need to take this woman to a hospital quickly," she called out.

40
00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:15.105
But no one wanted to help her.

41
00:03:15.106 --> 00:03:20.644
"Oh no! She smells too bad," said one passerby.

42
00:03:20.645 --> 00:03:24.844
"Just leave her there. She will die soon anyway," said another.

43
00:03:24.845 --> 00:03:29.070
But Mother Teresa did not give up. "Do not be afraid.

44
00:03:29.071 --> 00:03:32.628
I will take you to the hospital," she told the woman.

45
00:03:32.629 --> 00:03:35.982
She carefully picked her up and helped her to the hospital.

46
00:03:35.983 --> 00:03:40.961
But even at the hospital, people were not willing to help.

47
00:03:40.962 --> 00:03:45.045
"Oh, take her away! She smells very bad!

48
00:03:45.046 --> 00:03:50.610
She is so dirty that she might not be good for the other patients here!" they said.

49
00:03:50.611 --> 00:03:58.273
"Oh please! You must help her! I will not leave until you help her!" Mother Teresa insisted.

50
00:03:58.274 --> 00:04:01.959
Finally a doctor and a nurse agreed to care for the woman.

51
00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:07.259
They did their best, but they could not make the woman well.

52
00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:12.885
This made Mother Teresa very sad, but she did not stop helping other poor people.

53
00:04:12.886 --> 00:04:16.958
Many people in India thought Mother Teresa was wasting her time.

54
00:04:16.959 --> 00:04:20.325
"Ha! Look at that European!" they said.

55
00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:24.632
"What does she think she can do? There are too many poor people to help.

56
00:04:24.633 --> 00:04:29.247
She's foolish if she thinks she can make a difference."

57
00:04:29.248 --> 00:04:32.050
Mother Teresa, however, never gave up.

58
00:04:32.051 --> 00:04:38.341
Because of her tireless work, the people in the slums began to realize how much she cared for them.

59
00:04:38.342 --> 00:04:42.822
She taught them how to read and write and looked after them when they were sick.

60
00:04:42.823 --> 00:04:49.854
The poorest of the poor respected her, and over time others admired her too.

61
00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:57.640
In 1950 the pope gave her permission to start her own Catholic organization called the Missionaries of Charity.

62
00:04:57.641 --> 00:05:08.137
Many joined the Missionaries of Charity, becoming nuns and priests, to help Mother Teresa look after the poor in India and elsewhere in the world.

63
00:05:08.138 --> 00:05:13.153
In 1979 the world recognized Mother Teresa's tireless love.

64
00:05:13.154 --> 00:05:15.844
She was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize.

65
00:05:15.845 --> 00:05:22.603
When Mother Teresa was told she had won the prize, she simply said, "I am not worthy."

66
00:05:22.604 --> 00:05:29.306
Mother Teresa kept working until her death in 1997 at the age of 87.

67
00:05:29.307 --> 00:05:32.928
She was a warmhearted, caring, and deeply spiritual person.

68
00:05:32.929 --> 00:05:36.840
Her love for the poor has inspired many to follow in her footsteps.

69
00:05:36.841 --> 00:05:47.692
Since it was founded, the Missionaries of Charity has grown, and it now helps the poorest of the poor in almost every country in the world.

